# iconic-ui — shared layer rules

This repo is a **Nuxt layer** extended by iconic-panel (RMS + CRM) and iconic-engine. It owns:
- the design tokens (`app/assets/css/main.css`) — the HILO brand book scale: `--hilo-blue-*`, `--neutral-*`, `--bg-*`, `--fg-*`, `--border-*`, `--radius-*`, `--shadow-*`. Legacy names (`--forest*`, `--coral*`, `--ivory`, `--iv62`, `--iv38`, `--hair`, `--sand`, `--olive`, `--ok`, `--warn`) alias those tokens. Easing: `--ease`, `--eo`, `--eio`
- the mapping of those tokens onto Nuxt UI's variables (`--ui-bg*`, `--ui-text*`, `--ui-border*`, `--ui-primary`, `--ui-radius: 8px`)
- the Nuxt UI component overrides (`app.config.ts`) — cards at 16px, controls at 8px, hairline borders, brand shadows. The engine only increases button padding
- Satoshi from Fontshare, weights 300, 400, 500, 700, and 900. Loaded by the stylesheet in `nuxt.config.ts` and by the `@nuxt/fonts` family entry
- colour mode: **light is the default**. Dark uses the brand book's dark tokens
- shared components, prefixed **`Ank`** (`AnkLabel`, `AnkPill`, `AnkPanel`, `AnkKpi`, `AnkMoney`, `AnkThemeToggle`…)
- composables: `useApi()`, `useMoney()`, `useDates()`
- generated API types (`app/types/api.d.ts`, from iconic-api's OpenAPI spec)

## Rules
- Nothing app-specific here. If only one app uses it, it belongs in that app. Exception: a component two apps will share soon.
- Paths in `nuxt.config.ts` use `createResolver(import.meta.url)` so they resolve when extended.
- Every visual value comes from the HILO brand book (`../iconic-api/docs/brand/hilo-brand-book.html`). Do not invent a second palette or a second typeface.
- Keep `@nuxt/ui` and `tailwindcss` versions identical to the three apps.
- The `.playground` app contains a **style guide page** showing every token, every themed Nuxt UI component and every `Ank*` component in both themes. Update it whenever you add or change something.
- Apps (panel, engine, portal) extend this layer via the local path `../iconic-ui`. How they fetch it remotely is decided later with the git host.
- Quality: local `lint`, `typecheck`, `test` and `build` must pass.
- Releases: semantic version git tags (`v0.1.0`, `v0.2.0`…). Breaking changes bump the minor while < 1.0. Write a line in `CHANGELOG.md` per release.
